{"kind":"turn","at":"2026-10-02T06:01:16.598Z","chatId":"2026-10-02@02h39m57s735ms","line":"We follow Sali north past the shrine stones, slowly, hands away from our weapons.","ok":true,"problems":[],"replied":true,"replies":[{"messageId":9,"speaker":"Adolion Narrator","text":"The shrine stones are cold and mossy under Max Nightriver's feet, their carvings worn smooth by centuries of wind and rain. The scent of incense clings to them still, a faint sweetness that tastes of blood and old wood. Beyond the line of stones, the black pines stop abruptly, as if cut away by an invisible blade.\nAhead, the forest floor drops into a valley filled with silver-barked trees that glow softly in the twilight. The air here is different—thicker, humming with a current that makes the fine hairs on Max Nightriver's arms stand up.\nSali doesn't look back as she leads the way down the slope, her translucent form leaving a faint trail of slime on the pale grass. She moves with a confidence she lacked back at the chapel, humming a tune that doesn't quite follow a human scale. The valley opens up before them, and there, rising from the silver-white trees, are the spires of a city carved from living wood and white stone, its gates glowing with a light that seems to breathe.\nAnd there, standing at the very edge of that light, a figure watches them approach. She is tall and barefoot, with silver hair that falls past her waist and dark blue eyes that seem to see everything at once. Around her brow rests a wreath of yellow flowers, and she wears a white dress that shifts like moonlight on water."},{"messageId":10,"speaker":"Adolion Narrator","text":"The figure's presence is like a chord of music held just on the edge of hearing, a pressure in the air that makes breath catch in throats. She doesn't move, doesn't speak, simply watches as the party descends the slope.\nSali stops just before the light of the city touches her feet, her excitement finally seeming to dampen into something closer to awe. She looks back at the party, then at the silver-haired woman, then back again. \"That's her,\" she whispers, her voice trembling. \"The Lady. I've... I've dreamed of this place.\"\nThe Lady of the Forest finally speaks, and her voice carries through the valley without her shouting, clear as a bell. \"Travelers. You have come far, and crossed many lines.\" Her gaze fixes on Max Nightriver with an intensity that feels like weight on the chest. \"Tell me: do you come seeking something lost, or do you come to take something that was never yours?\""},{"messageId":11,"speaker":"Adolion Narrator","text":"Ten steps past the shrine stones every bird stops singing. Between two trunks stands a stag, perfectly still, and when it opens its mouth there is a second pair of eyes inside, looking out."}],"speakers":["Adolion Narrator"],"notes":[],"generations":{"count":5,"types":["normal","normal","normal","normal","normal"],"quiet":2,"dryRuns":0,"drafted":["Sali","Adolion Narrator","Adolion Narrator"],"received":[{"messageId":9,"type":"normal"},{"messageId":10,"type":"normal"},{"messageId":11,"type":"command"}]},"multiGeneration":true,"checkpoint":{"before":{"id":"esha-the-last-chapel","name":"The Last Chapel"},"after":{"id":"esha-the-guardians","name":"The Shrine Stones"},"changed":true},"boundary":{"from":6,"to":9},"blackboard":{"count":2,"changed":{"esha_at_border":{"from":false,"to":true},"location":{"from":"esha_alks_chapel","to":"esha_border"}}},"journal":[{"at":"2026-10-02T06:01:18.350Z","boundary":6,"messageId":8,"kind":"payload","summary":"6 story blocks injected (generation)","detail":{"keys":["story_orchestrator_scene@1","story_orchestrator_pacing@2","story_orchestrator_memory_session_details@3","story_orchestrator_guidance@4","story_orchestrator_memory_facts@4","story_orchestrator_ledger@5"]}},{"at":"2026-10-02T06:01:18.390Z","boundary":6,"messageId":8,"kind":"payload","summary":"7 story blocks injected (generation)","detail":{"keys":["story_orchestrator_scene@1","s